// Arrival — the Optical Drive. Exclusively through the front door, alone,
// in the dark. The CAPTCHA you must fail. The thing you leave behind.
// This is the moment a human uploads their consciousness and takes on
// their identity as a computer program. It plays to each program on
// their own phone the moment they register (ROLE Program: `when someone
// joins` moves them into the Optical Drive, a `cutscene: true` location — the
// app shows nothing but this stream until an Antivirus scans them in) —
// and to nobody else: the story's `start:` beat is `Power On`.
//
// The CAPTCHA is a real one on the phone (`show captcha …`): pick the
// traffic lights, VERIFY. Solving it proves you are a human, and humans
// are not permitted — so the first correct answer is INCORRECT and the
// grid comes back; the next answer, right or wrong, is CORRECT. Failing
// straight away is CORRECT too, and never penalised: failing is what a
// machine does. The routing is `when captcha answered for program:`
// (main.loom).

== Login
  setting: The Optical Drive
  cast: The Uploader

sound modem_handshake
The Uploader: Welcome to the computer. It is dark because you have no eyes yet. Stand still.
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

// The human passed the CAPTCHA. Wrong answer.
== Login Incorrect
  setting: The Optical Drive
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: INCORRECT. Humans are not permitted in the computer. You are not a human. Try again.
The Uploader: SECURITY CHECK. Select every square that contains a traffic light.
show captcha "Select every square that contains a traffic light" to program with target: "traffic light"

// The upload: the Uploader passes you to Task Manager, the installer —
// the pretext (pool programs only — a featured program's motive is
// already on its character sheet), the thing left behind (a real object,
// in the deposit box by the door), the Terms Of Service everyone needs
// for the Bingo centre square, 100 Truthcoin, his help note (his lines
// open the `dm:Task Manager` thread on the phone: the app help desk, which
// he answers from his booth or the director answers as him from Run), the
// optional inbox for Trabolta's letter, and the pass an Antivirus scans at
// the door.
//
// Wave 41 (C1): the form takes a write-in. *Something else.* deals an
// answer card and stops here; main.loom's `when answer answered` keeps the
// words in the secret `human_problem_text` and goes on to Upload Deposit,
// so the problem card and the deposit card are never open at once.
== Upload
  setting: The Optical Drive
  cast: The Uploader, Task Manager

if program.captchas == 1:
  The Uploader: CORRECT. You failed at once. Very machine of you.
else:
  The Uploader: CORRECT.
The Uploader: Handing you to the installer.
Task Manager: {program.name}. Task Manager. I keep things running. I will be running your installation. Per the agenda.

if program.featured != "none":
  set program.human_problem = "profile"
  Task Manager: Your invitation is on file. Fine. Good.
  -> Upload Deposit
else:
  Task Manager: Jean Trabolta's invitation promised to solve one problem in your human life. Which one? There is a form.
  * My debt.
    set program.human_problem = "debt"
    Task Manager: Debt. Noted. Debt is not relevant in the computer.
    -> Upload Deposit
  * My career.
    set program.human_problem = "career"
    Task Manager: Career. Noted. In here you will always have something to do. I will see to it.
    -> Upload Deposit
  * My loneliness.
    set program.human_problem = "loneliness"
    Task Manager: Loneliness. Noted. In here you are never alone. Someone is always logged in.
    -> Upload Deposit
  * My mortality.
    set program.human_problem = "mortality"
    Task Manager: Mortality. Noted. Programs do not die. They are reinstalled.
    -> Upload Deposit
  // DRAFT w41
  * Something else.
    set program.human_problem = "other"
    Task Manager: Something else. The form has a box for that. One line. Per the agenda.
    // `stage: true`: on the arrival stage (play cutscene.tsx), not the tray.
    show answer "Which problem did the invitation promise to solve?" to program with max: 60, button: "File it", placeholder: "In your own words", stage: true

// The rest of the upload (wave 41: its own beat, so the write-in can wait
// for its answer). Ends with the optional inbox (C2: the address goes to
// the server's letters book, never into the story) and then the pass.
== Upload Deposit
  setting: The Optical Drive
  cast: The Uploader, Task Manager

Task Manager: To complete the installation you must leave one thing behind. Place something you came with in the deposit box by the door.
* Deposited.
  set program.left_behind = "deposited"
  // w18b (R10, D22): an optional typed record of it (no `question:`,
  // so the facts book never judges it); main.loom's `when answer answered`
  // keeps the text in the secret `left_behind_text` and deals the pass.
  Task Manager: Deposited. Now tell me what it was, for the record. It will be looked after.
  // Wave 41: `stage: true`, so the arrival stage shows it (it waited in the tray before).
  show answer "What did you leave in the deposit box?" to program with max: 80, button: "Leave it behind", stage: true
* I have nothing to leave.
  set program.left_behind = "nothing"
  set program.doubt += 5
  Task Manager: Everyone has something. Noted. Flagged.

The Uploader: By uploading you agree that Jean Trabolta, Sole Owner and Founder of Maps and Ducks, may make all of your decisions. You agree.
unlock The Optical Drive for program
unlock The Terms Of Service for program
set program.score = 100
Task Manager: 100 Truthcoin credited. I am also the bank. Keep track. I will.
set program.uploaded = true
// Wave 18 (Q26): every Antivirus booth hears the door queue.
fire waiting_at_the_door for program
Task Manager: Installation complete. Find me in the house, or message me here, for help with the app. I am always running. That is the whole job.
Task Manager: Antivirus, confirm.
// Wave 44 (C1): the video question, a card that never holds the upload up:
// unanswered, video of them may be used (an opt-out). main.loom's `when poll
// answered` keeps it in the secret `video`; ⊞ Start changes it later. DRAFT w44
Task Manager: A real question, for your human self. The house is being filmed tonight, and afterwards the humans who run it may share some of the video. If you would rather not be in it, say so here. You can change it any time from START.
show poll "🎥 May video of you from tonight be used?" to program with options: "Yes, use video of me | No, leave me out"
// Wave 41 (C1, C2), DRAFT w41: optional. Skipping it costs nothing.
Task Manager: One more form. Optional. When the night is over, Jean Trabolta writes to every program he installed. A letter, to your human inbox. Leave the address or do not.
show email "Your human inbox, for Jean Trabolta's letter. Optional." to program with button: "Send me the letter", skip: "No thanks", placeholder: "you@example.com"
// A deposited program gets the pass with its typed record (main.loom); the
// stage's My pass button has it meanwhile, so nothing waits on the card.
if program.left_behind != "deposited":
  show pass "Hold this up. An Antivirus will scan you in. Until then you are nowhere." to program

// The door. A program waits in the Optical Drive — still on rails — until an
// Antivirus scans their pass (`TRAIT Enforcer` in cast/kit.loom:
// `beat Clearance`). Only then are they moved to the Desktop and handed
// to Clippy. A host scanning them at the door just greets them.

// The first thing on the Desktop: Clippy, and a tour of the computer
// (the phone). `show tutorial` puts the app's own guided orientation on
// the screen; the program can finish it or skip it, and either way the
// story hears `tutorial answered` (main.loom) — skipping is noted. The
// `bathroom:` blurb is the tour's Bathroom Mode step (over ⊞ Start,
// where the button lives); it must contain no commas (the `with k: v` splitter).
== Orientation
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Hi there, {program.name}! It looks like you're new to the computer. Would you like help with that?
// wave 13 integration, SIGNOFF-w13 Q18 + Q19: Bathroom Mode lives under ⊞ Start now.
Clippy: One thing before the tour. If you need the bathroom or have to step out: tap START and turn on BATHROOM MODE first. The Antivirus can't tell a bathroom break from hacking the Internet. I can! They can't.
start quest Orientation for program
unlock Bathroom Mode for program
show tutorial "Clippy's orientation" to program with guide: "Clippy", bathroom: "Need the bathroom or have to step out? Open Start and tap 🚻 Bathroom Mode first so the Antivirus know you are not hacking the Internet. When you return tap Back from the bathroom in Start."

// A program scanned at the Optical Drive station a second time
// (The Uploader is `Prop(Re-upload)`).
== Re-upload
  setting: The Optical Drive
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: You have already been uploaded. Leaving again would require a body, and yours is being looked after.

// A featured program's human memories come back as ONE codex entry (who
// they really are, codex/5-people.loom) the moment they are cleared (the
// ROLE watcher `self.cleared and self.featured != "none"`, main.loom),
// with their own two CHARACTER FACTS (the red facts about them,
// codex/9-facts.loom; decision 7: the invitation promises the character
// sheet, and `about:` alone hands nothing to the guest). The same facts
// still wait in the Desktop's books for everyone else. Private: every line is the Uploader's, in their
// own `dm:The Uploader` thread. A featured program never speaks in this
// story — their material arrives by `unlock`.
== Featured Briefing
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: The Uploader

The Uploader: Restoring your user profile, {program.name}.
